issues.body:
Try this code to reproduce the issue.       
 ```
        String htmlContent = "<div id=\"first\" 1=\"1\" 2=\"2\" 3=\"3\" 4=\"4\"></div>";
        Document doc = Jsoup.parse(htmlContent);
        Node startNode = doc.getElementById("first");
        Attributes attrs = startNode.attributes();
        Iterator<Attribute> iter = attrs.iterator();
        while(iter.hasNext()) {
            Attribute attr = iter.next();
            String attrName = attr.getKey();
            System.out.println(attrName + "=" + attr.getValue());
            startNode.removeAttr(attrName);
        }
```
Expected output
```
id=first
1=1
2=2
3=3
4=4
```
Actual output
```
id=first
2=2
4=4
```
It's working as expected with jsoup-1.9.2 and older jars.

